1
00:03:06,206 --> 00:03:12,206
...He's down but not out.

2
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:18,413
Jack Irish: Bad Debts is a crime, drama, mystery
film directed by Jeffrey Walker.

3
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:24,620
Jack Irish is a man getting his life back together again.

4
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:30,827
A former criminal lawyer whose world imploded, he now spends his days as a part-time investigator, debt
collector, apprentice cabinet maker, punter and sometime lover - the complete man really.

5
00:15:31,034 --> 00:15:37,034
Jack is an expert in finding those who don't want to be found - dead or alive.

6
00:18:37,241 --> 00:18:43,241
He helps out his mates while avoiding the past.

7
00:21:43,448 --> 00:21:49,448
That is until the past finds him.

8
00:24:49,655 --> 00:24:55,655
Jack Irish, played by Guy Pearce.

9
00:27:55,862 --> 00:28:01,862
Linda Hillier, played by Marta Dusseldorp.

10
00:31:02,068 --> 00:31:08,068
Cam Delray, played by Aaron Pedersen.

11
00:34:08,275 --> 00:34:14,275
Harry Strang, played by Roy Billing.

12
00:37:14,482 --> 00:37:20,482
Drew Greer, played by Damien Richardson.

13
00:40:20,689 --> 00:40:26,689
Barry Tregear, played by Shane Jacobson.

14
00:43:26,896 --> 00:43:32,896
Jack Irish is an Australian television drama series first
broadcast on ABC TV on 14 October 2012.

15
00:46:33,103 --> 00:46:39,103
The series stars Guy Pearce as the title character, a former
criminal lawyer turned investigator and debt collector.

16
00:49:39,310 --> 00:49:45,310
Much of the action is set in the Melbourne suburb of Fitzroy.

17
00:52:45,517 --> 00:52:51,517
Adapted from the crime fiction novels by author Peter Temple, the telemovies and series Jack
Irish were developed by Andrew Anastasios, Matt Cameron and Andrew Knight.

18
00:55:51,724 --> 00:55:57,724
They began as three feature-length movies, before being adapted into three
six-episode series, the final one airing from June 2021.

19
00:58:57,931 --> 00:59:03,931
All three movies were directed by Jeffrey Walker, while Kieran
Darcy-Smith serves as lead director on the series.

20
01:02:04,137 --> 01:02:10,137
Bad Debts, the first of the three feature-length movies, was watched by an average of 950,000
Australian viewers, ranking as the sixth most watched programme of the week.

21
01:05:10,344 --> 01:05:16,344
Black Tide, the second movie, was watched by an average of 851,000 Australian
viewers, ranking as the thirteenth most watched programme of the week.

22
01:08:16,551 --> 01:08:22,551
Dead Point, the third and final movie, was watched by an average of 780,000 Australian
viewers, ranking as the eleventh most watched programme of the week.

23
01:11:22,758 --> 01:11:28,758
The first series of six episodes broadcast from 11 February to 17 March 2016.

24
01:14:28,965 --> 01:14:34,965
The second series broadcast from 8 July to 12 August 2018.

25
01:17:35,172 --> 01:17:41,172
The second series was dedicated to the memory of
Peter Temple, who died in March 2018.

26
01:20:41,379 --> 01:20:47,379
The third and final series, Jack Irish: Hell Bent,
premiered on ABC TV and ABC iview on 13 June 2021.

27
01:23:47,586 --> 01:23:53,586
The film explores themes of grenade, client, melbourne,
australia, debt collector, police corruption.

28
01:26:53,793 --> 01:26:59,793
The tone is emotional and mind_bending.
